Getting at the data means doing the job

A job somebody declared — validating a batch, clearing a consignment — names
who may perform it, drawn as an active role in the tenant's own records. The
job reaches only the documents it needs and the ones it may change, and no
others; performing it leaves behind what it read and changed, when, on whose
authority, and what it was for. All three sit inside one tenant, which is its
own database, and the party running the deployment holds the copies without
being able to read them.
